{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.burgers_core_strain_cap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.burgers_core_strain_cap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.cap_eq_model_saturation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.cap_eq_model_saturation","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/burgers_core_strain_cap.lean#L101-L110","doc":"**The cap is the model's saturation value**: under the two-regime\nmodel's stretching normalization `V₁ = 4a²`, the derived cap\n`Γ/(4πa²)` reads exactly `Γ/(π·V₁)` — the phase-2 strain of\n`rem:hyperbolic-overlap-saturation`.  The saturation *value* is\nthereby derived from the Gaussian (exact-NS) profile up to this\nnormalization convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.coreStrain_le_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.coreStrain_le_cap","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/burgers_core_strain_cap.lean#L79-L99","doc":"**The finite-core strain cap**: for every distance `r > 0` the\nGaussian-core strain is at most `Γ/(4πa²)`.  From\n`1 − e^{−x} ≤ x` (Mathlib `Real.add_one_le_exp`) applied at\n`x = r²/(2a²)` — the `r`-dependence cancels exactly.  This is the\nsaturation: the approach can no longer amplify the strain once the\nseparation is inside the core. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.pointStrain_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.pointStrain_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/burgers_core_strain_cap.lean#L61-L77","doc":"**The singular vortex's strain is unbounded on approach**: for every\nlevel `M > 0` there is a positive distance at which the point-vortex\nstrain exceeds it (namely `r = √(Γ/(4πM))`, where the strain is\nexactly `2M`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.coreStrain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.coreStrain","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/burgers_core_strain_cap.lean#L55-L59","doc":"Co-rotation strain of a Gaussian-core vortex (Lamb–Oseen / Burgers\nprofile, core variance `a²`) at distance `r`:\n`Γ/(2πr²)·(1 − exp(−r²/(2a²)))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.pointStrain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.BurgersStrainCap.pointStrain","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/burgers_core_strain_cap.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Co-rotation strain of a singular point vortex at distance `r`:\n`Γ/(2πr²)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}